ne-man band debuted in 2004 with the self-published extended play, Short Cake, which caught the attention of the Korean indie label Pastel Music and released a trilogy of studio albums: Very Very Nice! and Short Cake (2005), Purple Drop (2006) and Baby Love (2007), which became his first charting record. After several years of hiatus, he released his next album in 2012 and has since released six more albums. Guest vocalists, notably the late Lee Jin-hwa (aka Humming Girl) and Shina-E, have appeared on many of Humming Urban Stereo's songs.","title":"Humming Urban Stereo","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Humming_Urban_Stereo"}},"Q11266766":{"id":"Q11266766","name":"Lee Min-hyuk","ko":"이민혁","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Minhyuk"],"birth":"1990-11-29","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","songwriter","rapper","record producer","actor","disc jockey"],"debut":"2012","agencies":[{"name":"Cube Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q484449","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q491067","name":"BtoB","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/btob_2mh/","x":"https://x.com/btob2mh","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/99fcd732-b610-4167-8008-5a900414eb47"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Lee Min-hyuk, commonly known as Minhyuk or Huta, is a South Korean rapper, singer, songwriter, actor, and presenter. He is a member of the South Korean boy group BtoB. He has appeared in multiple supporting roles in television series such as A New Leaf and Sweet, Savage Family.","title":"Lee Min-hyuk (rapper, born 1990)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lee_Min-hyuk_%28rapper%2C_born_1990%29"}},"Q114554574":{"id":"Q114554574","name":"Oh Ga-eun","ko":"오가은","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Gaeun"],"birth":"2005-11-08","death":"","birthplace":"","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["pop singer"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q114554468","